<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Chapter 36 — OAuth 2.1, OIDC & JWT.
    json/         strict minimal JSON (claims, JWKS, OAuth responses)
    jwt/          JWK, signing (the authorization server's side), verification (the resource server's side)
    discovery/    OpenID Connect discovery and a JWKS cache with rate-limited refresh for key rotation
    pkce/         RFC 7636 code verifier and S256 challenge
    exchange/     RFC 8693 token exchange: the authorization server's policy and the calling service's client
    authserver/   a small JDK-only authorization server for tests and measurements (not for production)
    web/          order-service as a resource server, and its token exchange for payment-service
  The protocol code has no framework dependencies; verify/run.sh compiles and measures it with a JDK alone.
-->
